 61MN c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2016Ba44:                          
 61MN c  Phys Lett B 760, 387 (2016)                                            
 61MN c  Compiled by G. G~urdal (SUNY Old Westbury College)                     
 61MN c  October 28, 2016                                                       
 61MN c  The {+61}Mn was produced by bombarding a uranium carbide target with   
 61MN2c  1.4 GeV proton beam at ISOLDE at CERN. The spectroscopic quadrupole    
 61MN3c  moment and the magnetic dipole moment of the ground state of {+61}Mn   
 61MN4c  were determined using the bunched-beam collinear laser spectroscopy    
 61MN5c  technique. The spectroscopic quadrupole moment and the magnetic        
 61MN6c  dipole moment of {+55}Mn (Q=+0.33 {I1} (from 1979De19) and             
 61MN7c  |m=+3.46871790 {I9} (from 1974Lu08, with corrections for diamagnetic   
 61MN8c  shielding)) were used as reference values. Comparison with             
 61MN9c  large-scale shell model calculations.                                  
 61MN cL E,J$From the Adopted Levels of {+61}Mn in the ENSDF database.          
 61MN  L 0.0          (5/2-)                                                    
 61MN2 L MOME2=+0.36 3$MOMM1=+3.535 2 (2016Ba44)                                
 61MN cL MOMM1,MOME2$from collinear laser spectroscopy                          
                                                                                
